1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,874
In this video, we'll set up an Orchard Core site.

2
00:00:03,874 --> 00:00:08,054
We'll answer the questions on the Setup screen, finish the setup, and sign

3
00:00:08,054 --> 00:00:09,830
in to the admin of the site.

4
00:00:14,430 --> 00:00:16,577
A site that is not set up is empty.

5
00:00:16,577 --> 00:00:19,563
When you open its address, you don't see a website.

6
00:00:19,563 --> 00:00:23,910
You see the Setup screen, which asks a few questions about the site you want.

7
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:29,034
Select Finish Setup, and Orchard Core builds the site from your answers.

8
00:00:29,034 --> 00:00:32,510
Then you sign in to the admin with the user you created.

9
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:38,494
Behind that button, Orchard Core checks the database, creates its tables, and runs

10
00:00:38,494 --> 00:00:42,716
the recipe, which turns on features and can add starting content.

11
00:00:42,716 --> 00:00:47,950
It also saves the site name and time zone as settings, and creates the super user.

12
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:53,968
This is the Setup screen.

13
00:00:53,968 --> 00:00:58,116
At the top right, Change language reloads it in another language.

14
00:00:58,116 --> 00:01:01,914
The whole form is on this one page, from the site name down

15
00:01:01,914 --> 00:01:03,317
to the super user.

16
00:01:03,786 --> 00:01:05,514
What is the name of your site?

17
00:01:05,514 --> 00:01:08,250
The answer becomes the default title of your pages.

18
00:01:08,250 --> 00:01:09,786
Let's type Contoso Bakery.

19
00:01:10,244 --> 00:01:15,688
Recipe sets how the site starts, by turning on features and sometimes adding content.

20
00:01:15,688 --> 00:01:19,396
Software as a Service is selected when the screen opens.

21
00:01:19,396 --> 00:01:23,344
Let's open the list, read the descriptions, and choose Blog.

22
00:01:23,847 --> 00:01:27,584
Default Time Zone sets how dates and times are shown and edited.

23
00:01:27,584 --> 00:01:29,987
Let's choose Los Angeles from the list.

24
00:01:30,464 --> 00:01:32,631
What type of database to use?

25
00:01:32,631 --> 00:01:37,523
Sqlite is selected, and it needs no database server or connection string.

26
00:01:37,523 --> 00:01:42,724
Orchard Core keeps a Sqlite database as a file in the data folder of the site.

27
00:01:44,324 --> 00:01:48,151
Sql Server, MySql, and Postgres use a database server.

28
00:01:48,151 --> 00:01:54,147
Create the database first, because Orchard Core creates the tables but not the database.

29
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:56,634
Then enter its Connection String.

30
00:01:57,384 --> 00:02:00,345
Table Prefix and Table Schema are optional.

31
00:02:00,345 --> 00:02:05,120
A prefix lets several sites share one database, and the default schema of

32
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:08,564
the server is used when you leave the schema blank.

33
00:02:09,314 --> 00:02:13,758
If setup can't finish, the screen returns with a message at the top.

34
00:02:13,758 --> 00:02:18,801
The connection string may be invalid, or the database, table prefix and schema

35
00:02:18,801 --> 00:02:20,483
may already be in use.

36
00:02:20,483 --> 00:02:22,824
Correct the answer and try again.

37
00:02:23,574 --> 00:02:27,583
Your host can preset some answers, such as the recipe or the database.

38
00:02:27,583 --> 00:02:31,539
When it does, the screen leaves those questions out, so your form can

39
00:02:31,539 --> 00:02:33,174
be shorter than this one.

40
00:02:37,438 --> 00:02:42,240
Below the database questions, the Super User section creates the first user.

41
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:46,340
The screen says this user has all the rights, and should be used

42
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:49,268
only during Setup and for disaster recovery.

43
00:02:49,727 --> 00:02:52,044
Enter a User Name and an Email.

44
00:02:52,044 --> 00:02:58,057
The user name accepts letters, digits, and the characters dash, dot, underscore, and plus.

45
00:02:58,508 --> 00:03:00,309
Select the Password field.

46
00:03:00,309 --> 00:03:04,360
A list shows the rules the password must meet, and checks each one

47
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,767
off as you meet it.

48
00:03:05,767 --> 00:03:08,468
A bar under the field shows your progress.

49
00:03:08,931 --> 00:03:12,212
Type the same password in Password Confirmation.

50
00:03:12,212 --> 00:03:16,951
The eye button beside each password field shows or hides what you typed.

51
00:03:17,432 --> 00:03:18,938
Select Finish Setup.

52
00:03:18,938 --> 00:03:24,322
Orchard Core checks the database, builds the site from your answers, and then opens it.

53
00:03:24,786 --> 00:03:28,271
This is the front end of the site, the part your visitors see.

54
00:03:28,271 --> 00:03:30,526
The name you entered is in the header.

55
00:03:34,742 --> 00:03:37,301
The admin is a separate part of the site.

56
00:03:37,301 --> 00:03:41,656
By default, you reach it by adding Admin to the end of the site's address.

57
00:03:41,656 --> 00:03:44,052
Orchard Core first asks you to log in.

58
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:49,163
In Username or email address, type the user name of the super user.

59
00:03:49,163 --> 00:03:51,000
Then type its password.

60
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:52,697
Select Log in.

61
00:03:52,697 --> 00:03:57,014
The admin opens with a welcome message and cards for first tasks:

62
00:03:57,014 --> 00:04:02,729
Create content, Customize theme, and Manage users, where you add users and assign roles.

63
00:04:02,729 --> 00:04:05,161
The menu leads to everything else.

64
00:04:05,619 --> 00:04:09,183
Setup saves your site name and time zone as settings.

65
00:04:09,183 --> 00:04:12,143
In the menu, select Settings, then General.

66
00:04:12,143 --> 00:04:17,639
There, Site name holds the name you entered, and Default Time Zone holds your choice.

67
00:04:18,093 --> 00:04:22,670
On the Resources tab, Use framework CDN is not selected, so the site

68
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:27,124
loads scripts and stylesheets, such as jQuery, from its own files.

69
00:04:27,124 --> 00:04:30,093
That works without an internet connection.

70
00:04:32,093 --> 00:04:33,567
That is the Setup screen:

71
00:04:33,567 --> 00:04:36,941
the questions it asks, what Finish Setup does, and how to sign in

72
00:04:36,941 --> 00:04:38,367
to the site you created.

73
00:04:38,367 --> 00:04:39,603
Thanks for watching.

